{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And his father rebuked him.</b> He wished to nullify the dream in the presence of his brothers, and therefore rebuked him, to abate their wrath against him." "<b>And he said, Shall we indeed come, I and your mother and your brothers.</b> Now your mother is already dead — just as it is impossible regarding your mother, so too the rest is nullified. Even so, ״ואביו שמר את הדבר״ — and his father kept the matter — for he knew the greatness of the dream and waited for it to be fulfilled, in the manner of what is written (Daniel 7:28): ״ומלתא בלבי נטרית״. And in Bereshit Rabbah: ״ואביו שמר את הדבר״ — the Holy Spirit says, keep the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:10.493749818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}